#   ONE CORRECTION TO THE STANDING SUGGESTION ABOVE, and the reason it is still
#   only filed. Four entries now say the honest fix is to hash this surface with
#   `///` lines stripped. That may be wrong, and it is worth someone checking
#   before it is built: this engine EXTRACTS doc comments -- they are indexed as
#   doc text and answered by `document`, `doc-drift` and hover. So a `///` edit
#   is not self-evidently invisible to extraction the way a whitespace change
#   is; it changes stored CONTENT while leaving stored PARSES alone. If that is
#   right, the two are different staleness questions and the remedy is not one
#   hash with comments stripped but a recognition that a doc edit needs a
#   REINDEX of the touched files, which the sweep already does with --reindex,
#   and never a version bump.
#
#   Not decided here, and deliberately not implemented here: changing this
#   guard's definition of identity as a side effect of the fifth sweep to trip
#   it would be exactly the move every entry above warns against.
#
#   The same warning as every entry above: if a future edit to these files ever
